{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the redeemed, etc.</b> These are the returning ones; they shall come to Zion with shouting, and everlasting joy upon their heads, because the force of the soul is in the head. And some say that they are like the form of a canopy over their heads; this too is sound." "<b>Gladness and joy shall overtake.</b> Them. And some say that they will pursue after the gladness and overtake it."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {0 "Resolved וי״א (ואפשר י״א?) as 'some say'; the reading is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:47.013100902Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}